//// Decision 127 of 1.0.10-beta (front 24, § Cells "Migration"; guide.md § 9,
//// row `#[@iterator]` / `#[@asyncGenerator]` / `@AsyncIterator`) — a wrapper
//// that had already left stays gone. Measured at compiler `82e32e36`: an
//// unknown `@Name<…>` is typed as an opaque nominal (`type mismatch: expected
//// AsyncIterator, …` at best, silence in a parameter). The cell asks for
//// `effect-type-removed`, the family's code with the fix-it
//// `@Stream<@Result<T, E>>` — decision 127 names no code for the older names;
//// reported as a choice. The new form is `run/stream_pages.bp`.

fn ticks(n: i32) -> @AsyncIterator<i32> {
    var i = 0;
    while (i < n) { yield i; i = i + 1; };
}

pub fn main() { ticks(2); }
